WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:24.962 --> 00:00:27.362
Hi, welcome back to Nagarjuna's course.

00:00:27.362 --> 00:00:29.403
Let's begin.

00:00:29.403 --> 00:00:32.130
This is Chapter 17,

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:33.869
LAS KYI BRTAGS PA.

00:00:33.869 --> 00:00:38.869
This is an investigation into the nature of karma

00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:42.000
and the seeds of karma.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:47.000
We took a look and
found this chapter rather unusual

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:52.050
because we finally understand what it's about,

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:53.875
and it doesn't even seem like Nagarjuna's style. Don't

00:00:53.875 --> 00:00:57.162
worry, he'll confuse us again later.

00:00:57.162 --> 00:00:59.320
I personally

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:02.450
kept wondering why he would discuss the

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:06.070
Abhidharma's introduction to karma

00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:09.980
and divide karma into motivation,

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:12.630
and motivated actions and words.

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:17.053
Then he talked about some obscure Abhidharma concepts

00:01:17.053 --> 00:01:22.053
about different types of karma.


00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:25.040
For example, you can see a person's motivation,

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:30.040
or an aura, or a kind of halo that forms around them,
whether good or bad.

00:01:30.073 --> 00:01:32.370
That's another kind of karma. Does

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:35.004
someone want to earn $100?

00:01:35.004 --> 00:01:40.004
Guess why he's talking about
these obscure and difficult-to-understand concepts of karma in the Abhidharma.

00:01:41.285 --> 00:01:44.818
[A faint voice of reply]

00:01:44.818 --> 00:01:48.401
No, why?
Why did he do that?

00:01:49.995 --> 00:01:52.912
[A faint voice of reply]

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:56.731
The answer is simpler than that.

00:01:56.731 --> 00:01:59.250
[Student] Because everyone is a student of Abhidharma.

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:01.191
Excellent! How much did I just say? One hundred US dollars?

00:02:01.191 --> 00:02:02.024
[Student] Yes,

00:02:02.024 --> 00:02:04.524
Patch got $100. Don't forget to tell Elizabeth. Yes, back

00:02:04.524 --> 00:02:06.450
then, for about seven hundred years,

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:08.160
everyone was a student of Abhidharma.

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:11.500
Then he tried to overturn that wave.

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:14.070
By the way, he actually did it, all by
himself.

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:15.523
He faced an

00:02:15.523 --> 00:02:20.010
endless ocean of Abhidharma "accountants"

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:23.426
and turned them all into hippies. Yeah. Okay,

00:02:23.426 --> 00:02:24.967


00:02:24.967 --> 00:02:27.229
he goes on.

00:02:27.229 --> 00:02:30.940
We want to know if you remember

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:33.510
why he didn't talk about the ten wholesome deeds

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:34.530
and the ten non-wholesome deeds.

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:37.181
Guess what he's going to do next?
Ready?

00:02:37.181 --> 00:02:39.256
,DKAR PO'I LAS KYI LAM BCU PO,

00:02:39.256 --> 00:02:40.956
,CHOS SGRUB PA YI THABS YIN TE, ,

00:02:40.956 --> 00:02:43.047
CHOS KYI 'BRAS BU 'DI GZHAN DU,

00:02:43.047 --> 00:02:46.012
,'DOD PA'I YON TAN RNAM LNGA'O,

00:02:46.012 --> 00:02:50.790
DKAR PO'I LAS refers to virtuous deeds or good deeds.

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:53.543
LAM BCU PO -- 10 paths,

00:02:53.543 --> 00:02:54.690
that is, ten kinds of virtuous deeds. The

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:57.597
ten precepts in Buddhism

00:02:57.597 --> 00:03:00.223
are called the ten virtuous paths.

00:03:01.799 --> 00:03:05.290
CHOS SGRUB ... CHOS SGRUB PA YI THABS

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:08.680
These are the methods to achieve the Dharma.

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:10.550
Then Master Chögyal says that the

00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:14.250
Dharma mentioned by the enlightened Nagarjuna here

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:19.250
refers to higher rebirth and ultimate

00:03:19.533 --> 00:03:22.380
goodness. Ultimate goodness is called NGES LEGS, which refers to

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:25.150
Nirvana and Buddhahood.

00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:28.410
In the first line and a half, Master Nagarjuna said that the ten

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:34.020
virtuous paths

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:36.730
are the methods to achieve the Dharma.

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:41.730
He refers to higher rebirth and Nirvana, as well as Buddhahood.

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:45.090
CHOS KYI 'BRAS BU 'DI GZHAN DU

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:46.660
Then this line says The

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:50.470
result of this Buddhist teaching is "this" and "that." Does

00:03:50.470 --> 00:03:54.490
anyone want to guess
what "this" and "that" refer to respectively?

00:03:54.490 --> 00:03:58.775
You will have a very good outcome in this life and future lives,

00:03:58.775 --> 00:03:59.975
dirstha-adirstha, right?

00:03:59.975 --> 00:04:03.438
In this life and in future lives, you will see

00:04:03.438 --> 00:04:05.330
'DOD PA'I YON TAN RNAM LNGA'O.

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:09.347
In particular, you will receive 'DOD PA'I YON TAN'

00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:13.210
good things in the desire realm:

00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:14.980
delicious food,

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:19.940
beautiful music, soft blankets.

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:24.250
Think about how wonderful your next life will be when you follow these 10 virtuous deeds.

00:04:24.250 --> 00:04:26.882


00:04:26.882 --> 00:04:29.846
How comfortable your life will be.

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:36.000
You will have expensive face cream.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:39.573
I don't know about you, but I'm starting to think

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:42.426
this is strange.

00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:45.920
This doesn't seem like something Nagarjuna would say.

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:49.300
You will get a new car.

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:51.105
Your hair will grow back.

00:04:51.105 --> 00:04:54.656
You will be full of energy, right?

00:04:54.656 --> 00:04:59.656
Then we learned from Master Qiu Ni that

00:05:00.010 --> 00:05:05.010
he was actually criticizing, do you understand?

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:07.140
He said, "Oh, that's great, the ten virtuous deeds."

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:11.490
- What?
- More money, more cars, more hair.

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:13.067
You'll be very healthy.

00:05:13.067 --> 00:05:16.970
Then we learn from Master Chuni that what

00:05:16.970 --> 00:05:21.593
Master Nagarjuna wanted to say was:

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:24.910
"Look at how people talk about karma.

00:05:24.910 --> 00:05:26.780
Look at how these people talk about karma.

00:05:26.780 --> 00:05:30.610
Look at where they want to put karma.

00:05:30.610 --> 00:05:33.730
He's criticizing them,

00:05:33.730 --> 00:05:36.910
and what he's criticizing goes
deeper than you can imagine.

00:05:36.910 --> 00:05:38.680
Getting a lot of money is good.

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:40.360
Getting a nice car is good.

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:42.130
Having a nice apartment is good.

00:05:42.130 --> 00:05:46.070
But if you think that the relationship between following the ten virtuous deeds and
getting those things

00:05:46.070 --> 00:05:50.230
is inherently real, then that's not right.

00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:52.843
- Is it okay to have a nice apartment?
- Yes.

00:05:52.843 --> 00:05:54.970
Can I have a lot of money in my bank account?

00:05:54.970 --> 00:05:57.410
Of course, that's fine, you can help more people.

00:05:57.410 --> 00:05:58.320
Can I have a big car?

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:02.080
Yes. You can take more people
to John Brady's house for a party

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:05.383
[laughs].

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:10.730
But if you think that the relationship between helping others

00:06:10.730 --> 00:06:12.600
or reciting the Medicine Buddha mantra

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:14.930
and getting all the good things

00:06:14.930 --> 00:06:16.560
is inherently real,

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:20.720
if you think that these connections don't come from you, then something's going to

00:06:20.720 --> 00:06:24.820
happen in the next verse. The

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:26.660
next verse reveals what

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:28.250
we're really thinking about.

00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:29.164
By the way, I like this,"

00:06:29.164 --> 00:06:34.164
Master Chuni said.
He added a comment next to the last sentence.

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:36.760
Here's a photo of

00:06:36.760 --> 00:06:39.400
this person holding a plane ticket.

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:41.390
He says, "By the way,

00:06:41.390 --> 00:06:45.730
this verse is basically criticizing those who

00:06:45.730 --> 00:06:49.580
focus on using karma to obtain things. It's

00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:52.020
not that these things themselves are wrong,

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:54.450
but rather that their feelings about the connection between karma and things are

00:06:54.450 --> 00:06:57.403
too deeply ingrained."

00:06:58.240 --> 00:07:00.420
They don't understand the emptiness of those connections themselves.

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:03.130
He says, "That's okay.

00:07:03.130 --> 00:07:07.690
We can add another line next to this verse and

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:10.830
say: You will get a house, you will have an apartment,

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:12.478
you will become healthy,

00:07:12.478 --> 00:07:15.227
and you will also attain enlightenment." [laughs]

00:07:15.227 --> 00:07:16.060
He says, "If it were me,

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:18.140
I would add another line to the verse.

00:07:18.140 --> 00:07:19.620


00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:22.790
So, notice that person holding a plane ticket and passport.

00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:27.063
That's the passport to enlightenment.

00:07:27.063 --> 00:07:30.380
This also comes from the ten wholesome deeds, okay?"

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:34.400
Then, the next verse reveals Nagarjuna's

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:35.880
view on the previous verse

00:07:37.782 --> 00:07:39.331
: GAL TE BRTAG PA DER 'GYUR NA,

00:07:39.331 --> 00:07:43.191
,NYES PA CHEN PO MANG POR 'GYUR,

00:07:43.191 --> 00:07:46.640
If you do BRTAG PA

00:07:46.640 --> 00:07:48.380
What is BRTAG PA?

00:07:48.380 --> 00:07:49.613
B-R-T-A-G

00:07:50.502 --> 00:07:53.494
ba rata ta BRTA ga BRTAG

00:07:53.494 --> 00:07:54.700
[Woman] Investigation

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:55.760
Yes, investigation

00:07:55.760 --> 00:08:00.730
If that's the

00:08:00.730 --> 00:08:03.627
best investigation you can do regarding karma

00:08:03.627 --> 00:08:05.210
NYES PA CHEN PO MANG PO

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:09.080
You'll get into a mountain

00:08:09.080 --> 00:08:11.520
of questions [laughs]

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:13.560
Nagarjuna... It's

00:08:13.560 --> 00:08:15.430
a bit like another person is looking at him and he says,

00:08:15.430 --> 00:08:17.450
um, I say you should do the ten virtuous deeds

00:08:17.450 --> 00:08:19.080
because you can get a lot of wealth.

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:21.760
He says, my God, think about it, is this how
you conduct investigations?

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:25.100
This is a huge problem, a really big problem.

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:27.330
Many problems will arise from this. You

00:08:27.330 --> 00:08:28.900
recite the Medicine Buddha mantra

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:31.320
because you think you will be healthier as a result, just for

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:34.633
that reason,

00:08:35.510 --> 00:08:37.300
and you believe there is such a connection between the mantra and health.

00:08:37.300 --> 00:08:38.690


00:08:38.690 --> 00:08:41.680
NYES PA CHEN PO MANG POR 'GYUR,

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:44.550
then you will fall into many problems afterward,

00:08:44.550 --> 00:08:45.615
such as...?

00:08:45.615 --> 00:08:47.339
,DE LTA BAS NA BRTAG PA DE,

00:08:47.339 --> 00:08:49.170
,'DIR NI 'THAD PA MA YIN NO,

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:50.610
Master Nagarjuna further said,

00:08:50.610 --> 00:08:52.720
He said, Your kind of investigation

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:54.793
is a counter-investigation,

00:08:55.740 --> 00:08:56.573
okay?

00:08:56.573 --> 00:09:00.666
Your survey is a stupid survey.

00:09:00.666 --> 00:09:01.499
[Students laugh]

00:09:01.499 --> 00:09:02.332
Okay, understand?

00:09:02.332 --> 00:09:04.330
That's an idiotic investigation.

00:09:04.330 --> 00:09:05.163
What?

00:09:05.163 --> 00:09:07.330
You're using karma just to get some money,

00:09:07.330 --> 00:09:12.243
or just to cure hair problems or something.

00:09:12.243 --> 00:09:16.090
By the way, there's nothing wrong with getting money, and there's nothing wrong with

00:09:16.090 --> 00:09:19.100
wanting more hair. The mistake is

00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:23.373
assuming there's an automatic connection between them. The key is


00:09:23.373 --> 00:09:25.880
how you perceive the mantra,

00:09:25.880 --> 00:09:27.547
not the mantra itself.

00:09:27.547 --> 00:09:29.000
Okay,

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:32.653
here are two children.

00:09:33.690 --> 00:09:35.636
They're twins.

00:09:38.980 --> 00:09:41.280
When you see them,

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:43.800
you might guess it's a picture of twins.

00:09:43.800 --> 00:09:45.210
But that's just an assumption.

00:09:45.210 --> 00:09:46.870
They might not be twins at all;

00:09:46.870 --> 00:09:50.870
they might just look alike. In other

00:09:50.870 --> 00:09:54.490
words, you chant a mantra, and something
might happen afterward,

00:09:54.490 --> 00:09:56.980
but is there a connection between the two? Is it

00:09:56.980 --> 00:10:00.292
really as it appears to you?

00:10:00.292 --> 00:10:01.300
Okay, let's move

00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:04.628
on to the next section.

00:10:08.521 --> 00:10:10.245
SANGS RGYAS RNAMS DANG RANG RGYAL DANG,

00:10:10.245 --> 00:10:11.545
,NYAN THOS RNAMS KYIS GANG GSUNGS PA'I,

00:10:11.545 --> 00:10:13.679
,BRTAG PA GANG ZHIG 'DIR 'THAD PA,

00:10:13.679 --> 00:10:16.050
,DE NI RAB TU BRJOD PAR BYA,

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:17.163
By the way,

00:10:18.300 --> 00:10:22.580
there's a survey about karma that

00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:24.020
you might have done,

00:10:24.020 --> 00:10:26.120
and it's a better survey

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:28.248
than a stupid one.

00:10:28.248 --> 00:10:30.670
You could have done a wise survey.

00:10:30.670 --> 00:10:32.490
Which one is it?

00:10:32.490 --> 00:10:35.520
Yes, the Buddha described it, the

00:10:35.520 --> 00:10:37.540
Pratyekabuddhas described it, and the

00:10:37.540 --> 00:10:40.110
Sravakas also spoke about it.
These are all Arhats,

00:10:40.110 --> 00:10:41.810
some who have attained Nirvana.

00:10:41.810 --> 00:10:45.930
If you want to conduct a karmic investigation,

00:10:45.930 --> 00:10:48.570
I suggest you follow their

00:10:48.570 --> 00:10:50.847
investigation instead of your own [laughs].

00:10:50.847 --> 00:10:51.680
Okay?

00:10:51.680 --> 00:10:54.190
Don't assume there's an inherent connection between the Medicine Buddha mantra

00:10:54.190 --> 00:10:57.480
and money or health.

00:10:57.480 --> 00:11:00.303


00:11:00.303 --> 00:11:02.800
I suggest you shift your investigation focus. Shift it to

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:03.890
where? How about we move on

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:07.220
to the one described by the Buddha

00:11:07.220 --> 00:11:08.099
?

00:11:08.099 --> 00:11:09.530
Hmm, what is that?

00:11:09.530 --> 00:11:11.820
DE NI RAB TU BRJOD PAR BYA

00:11:11.820 --> 00:11:14.130
I'm about to tell you,

00:11:14.130 --> 00:11:17.157
I'll explain it to you perfectly.

00:11:17.157 --> 00:11:22.138
RAB TU means
I'll make sure you understand 100%.

00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:27.860
Then he started a very deep topic,
a very difficult topic.

00:11:27.860 --> 00:11:29.461
So finally,

00:11:29.461 --> 00:11:32.287
Nagarjuna took off the gloves,
Master Nagarjuna took off his gloves (rolled up his sleeves)

00:11:32.287 --> 00:11:34.330
to show you his true style. Let's

00:11:34.330 --> 00:11:35.720
begin. Buckle up.

00:11:35.720 --> 00:11:38.350


00:11:38.350 --> 00:11:39.766
Let's look at

00:11:39.766 --> 00:11:42.558
DPANG RGYA JI LTAR DE BZHIN CHUD

00:11:43.732 --> 00:11:44.940
, MI ZA

00:11:44.940 --> 00:11:47.132
, MI ZA LAS NI BU LON BZHIN.

00:11:47.132 --> 00:11:50.750
There are many problems with the engraving,

00:11:50.750 --> 00:11:52.300
but I understand.

00:11:52.300 --> 00:11:55.940
DPANG RGYA refers to a contract,

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:59.830
usually used for loans. Before

00:11:59.830 --> 00:12:03.130
2000, when you borrowed money, you

00:12:03.130 --> 00:12:05.030
had to sign a DPANG RGYA,

00:12:05.030 --> 00:12:08.930
or when you got married, you
had to sign a DPANG RGYA.

00:12:08.930 --> 00:12:11.250
So it can be a marriage contract

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:14.530
or a loan agreement.

00:12:14.530 --> 00:12:19.530
He said DPANG RGYA DE BZHIN

00:12:20.046 --> 00:12:23.088
DPANG RGYA JI LTAR DE BZHIN CHUD.

00:12:23.088 --> 00:12:24.600
You have to read across lines.

00:12:24.600 --> 00:12:27.488
You must say CHUD MI ZA.

00:12:27.488 --> 00:12:29.090
You know CHUD MI ZA. I've

00:12:29.090 --> 00:12:32.020
taught you this again and again in the Stages of the Path course. The Fourth Law of Karma:

00:12:32.020 --> 00:12:34.545


00:12:34.545 --> 00:12:37.820
BYAS PA CHUD MI ZA BA. The

00:12:37.820 --> 00:12:39.420
Fourth Law of Karma:

00:12:40.408 --> 00:12:45.408
If you do something, you will reap the consequences
(you reap what you sow).

00:12:46.029 --> 00:12:47.210
BYAS PA CHUD MI ZA BA.

00:12:47.210 --> 00:12:50.541
Literally, BYAS PA means that
if you do something,

00:12:50.541 --> 00:12:51.860
CHUD MI ZA BA means that

00:12:51.860 --> 00:12:55.010
it won't disappear over time.

00:12:55.010 --> 00:12:59.720
You can't expect that after you lied to your mother,

00:12:59.720 --> 00:13:03.078
and before 20 other people lied to you, the
karma will disappear before 20 people come back to lie to you. It's

00:13:03.078 --> 00:13:06.600


00:13:06.600 --> 00:13:08.040
impossible.

00:13:08.040 --> 00:13:12.310
You shouldn't hope that you've done something wrong,

00:13:12.310 --> 00:13:14.320
stay quiet, and not tell anyone.

00:13:14.320 --> 00:13:16.870
Eventually, everyone will forget

00:13:16.870 --> 00:13:20.293
because that's not how karma works.

00:13:20.293 --> 00:13:23.922
Everything is recorded,
everything spreads.

00:13:23.922 --> 00:13:28.922
So, he says this principle:

00:13:29.207 --> 00:13:30.877
CHUD MI ZA BA. Don't forget this word

00:13:30.877 --> 00:13:32.480
because we will talk about it again and again.

00:13:32.480 --> 00:13:33.570


00:13:33.570 --> 00:13:36.600
In this part, CHUD MI ZA BA

00:13:36.600 --> 00:13:40.610
in Western Chinese languages ​​refers to...

00:13:40.610 --> 00:13:42.860
Karma doesn't disappear automatically just because you wait long enough.


00:13:42.860 --> 00:13:44.670
In fact, quite the opposite.

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:46.700
Don't think that karma disappears out of thin air.

00:13:46.700 --> 00:13:51.700
Now, in Abhidharma,

00:13:51.890 --> 00:13:56.320
you can take general proof,
but in the Abhidharma school,

00:13:56.320 --> 00:13:59.300
this becomes a tool. The fact that

00:13:59.300 --> 00:14:01.970


00:14:01.970 --> 00:14:04.680
karma doesn't disappear out of thin air

00:14:04.680 --> 00:14:08.320
 
is a separate thing in the Abhidharma system. It

